{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789857046,"nonce":"XI5pl/lHpll0omnxW07fMm3LsB0=","message":"Spec and checklist landed in doc/design/bridges/jira-sandbox.md (3ccc0a5a). The task stays open: creating the site needs an Atlassian account.\n\nThe ask in short: two projects on one free site — A shaped like the company's Jira (real issue types, a custom workflow with at least one status whose NAME does not match its CATEGORY, non-universal transitions, sprints incl. one closed), B shaped like Linear (Initiative/Project/Issue, cycles, no sub-tasks). B exists so a schema preset that works for both cannot be accidental.\n\nHighest-value first step is not the site itself, it's the sanitized schema dump (fields, issue types, per-type statuses with categories, priorities, sprints) committed under bridge/jira/testdata/sandbox/. That is what 59fed1c builds the presets against and what lets bridge tests run in CI with no network and no secrets. Phase 3 is buildable off the fixtures alone.","files":null}]}